    The same gate read through Delta_tau, which has no estimator floor.
    The prereg's own Step A is I_C^(3) = (1/128)[sum p_s^-1](Delta_tau)^2 +
    O(Delta_tau^3), so Delta_tau ~ h^1 IS the h^2 gate, measured on a moment
    instead of on an entropy difference.  The 2D sibling read it this way too
    (Delta_tau ~ h^1.000).  This is why the direct route above is unreadable:
    the h^2 regime is squeezed between the estimator floor below and the peak
    above, and at these sample sizes there is no window left between them.
    L=8   d ln|Delta_tau| / d ln u = +1.0799 (4 smallest u)  +0.9722 (6 smallest)   predicted 1.0000   FIRES
